# Mailbox is no longer a ForkJoinTask. A mailbox is one object that its dispatcher resubmits for the
# whole lifetime of the actor, and ForkJoinPool.execute pushes a ForkJoinTask as-is instead of
# wrapping it, so the same reference kept returning to the same work-queue slot. A steal that stalls
# between its base recheck and its slot CAS can then move the queue's base backwards and permanently
# damage the queue (https://github.com/ben-manes/caffeine/issues/2021), and a single exceptional
# completion made ForkJoinTask.doExec short-circuit forever, silently disabling the mailbox
# (https://github.com/apache/pekko/issues/3620). Mailbox is private[pekko] and escapes only through
# MessageDispatcher.createMailbox.
ProblemFilters.exclude[MissingTypesProblem]("org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Mailbox")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Mailbox.getRawResult()Unit")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Mailbox.setRawResult(scala.runtime.BoxedUnit)Unit")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("org.apache.pekko.dispatch.Mailbox.exec()Boolean")
